    <string name="privacy_policy_title">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_text">
<b>1. Local Data Storage</b>
All your books, reading progress, bookmarks, local chats, and interaction history are stored strictly on your device by Light Reader. We do not collect, transmit through our servers, or store your personal files on external servers.
<b>2. API Key Security</b>
The API keys you enter (Google Gemini, OpenAI, DeepSeek, OpenRouter) are encrypted using Android system tools (EncryptedSharedPreferences) and are stored exclusively in the device\'s secure storage.
<b>3. Data Transfer to Third-Party Services</b>
When sending requests to the AI assistant (including text fragments of books for RAG search), data is transmitted directly to your chosen provider (Google, OpenAI, DeepSeek, or OpenRouter) using your API key. We do not transmit your data through our servers; the transfer occurs directly from your device to the provider at your initiative. We do not act as intermediaries in this exchange and do not store logs of your requests.
<b>4. Device Permissions</b>
The app requests access to the file system solely to read, convert, and save local books and covers in the device\'s memory.
<b>5. Data Retention</b>
All local data, including books, reading progress, bookmarks, chats, cached embeddings, and settings, is stored on your device until you delete it or uninstall the application. API keys are stored until you delete them in the AI settings or uninstall the application.
<b>6. Deleting Your Data</b>
You can delete all app data by uninstalling the application. Uninstalling Light Reader removes all locally stored data from your device. You may also delete individual data, such as chat history or API keys, within the app.
<b>7. Analytics and Telemetry</b>
Light Reader does not collect analytics, telemetry, crash reports, or usage statistics. We do not use advertising identifiers or third-party tracking tools.
</string>



