    <string name="readme_title">README.md</string>
    <string name="readme_subtitle">Project description</string>

    <string name="readme_content" translatable="false" formatted="false"><![CDATA[
# Light Reader

This application is a modern mobile e-book reader powered by the **Readium Kotlin Toolkit** for the Android platform. The project combines essential book reading functionality, a built-in library, and advanced AI features.

---

## Key Features & Functionality

### 1. E-Book Reading & Supported Formats

* **Supported Formats:** EPUB, PDF, FB2, TXT, DOCX.
* **Built-in Converters:** Automatic conversion of FB2, TXT, and DOCX files to EPUB format for a comfortable reading experience.
* **Display Customization:** Adjustable fonts, text size, color themes (light/dark), quick settings menu, and visual preferences adaptation.
* **Navigation & Bookmarks:** Reading progress saving, bookmarking, text highlighting, and table of contents (Outline) navigation.
* **Text-to-Speech (TTS):** Book narration with playback control and voice customization.
* **Search:** In-text search within the opened book.

### 2. Bookshelf & Library Management

* **UI:** Modern book list interface built with Jetpack Compose.
* **Filtering & Tags:** Labeling books with "Favorite", "Want to Read", and "Read" statuses via the built-in `BookTagManager`.
* **Sorting & Metadata:** Displaying file size, date added, format type, and reading progress percentage.
* **Cover Generation:** Automatic creation of text-based and graphic covers when missing.

### 3. Artificial Intelligence Integration (AI Assistant)

The application features an AI assistant that allows users to analyze book content, ask questions, and engage in contextual dialogue with the loaded work.

* **Supported AI Providers:**
* **Google Gemini** (direct integration with full-text analysis).
* **OpenAI** (models like `gpt-4o-mini` and the embeddings subsystem).
* **DeepSeek** (`deepseek-chat` models and local/cloud variants).
* **OpenRouter** (access to a wide range of third-party models).

* **RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation):**
* Text chunking with custom overlap settings.
* Generation and caching of text vector embeddings.
* Retrieval of the most relevant book passages using cosine similarity for accurate AI responses based on the content.

* **Chat Management:**
* JSON-based chat history persistence.
* Creating, renaming, and deleting chat sessions.
* Exporting chats to `.txt` format and sharing results.
* Attaching a specific library book to the active chat session.
]]></string>
























